    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The numerator is \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\frac{a^2+x^2-(x^2-a^2)} {\\sqrt{a^2+x^2}}\\\\ &\\qquad{}=\\frac{2a^2}{\\sqrt{a^2+x^2}}. \\end{aligned} \\] Dividing by \\(a^2+x^2\\) gives \\[ \\frac{2a^2}{(a^2+x^2)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine the two terms in the numerator over a common denominator",
        "The new numerator simplifies to \\((a^2+x^2)-(x^2-a^2)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
